=========================================================
CLASS DESIGN (OOAD) – INTERVIEW NOTES (COPYABLE)
=========================================================

Class Design is the process of converting requirements into classes, objects, attributes, methods, and relationships.

Goal:
-----
Create a design that is:
• Simple
• Maintainable
• Extensible
• Reusable
• Loosely Coupled
• Highly Cohesive

=========================================================
STEP 1. UNDERSTAND REQUIREMENTS
=========================================================

Before writing classes, clarify the requirements.

Ask questions like:

• What features are required?
• What are the constraints?
• Any assumptions?
• Number of users?
• Concurrency?
• Future extensibility?

Example (Parking Lot)

Requirements

• Multiple floors
• Different parking spots
• Car, Bike, Truck support
• Entry and Exit gates
• Ticket generation
• Payment
• Display available spots

Never jump directly into coding.

Always clarify requirements first.



